{"r":"vxn","lane":{"p":332,"e":[{"h":"ثَخُنَ","t":["(T, S, M, Msb, K,) aor. ; (K;) and ",[2,"ثَخَنَ"],", (El-Ahmar, ISd, Msb, TA,) aor. ; (TA;) inf. n. ",[2,"ثَخَانَةٌ"]," (T, S, Msb, K, &c.) and ",[2,"ثُخُونَةٌ"]," (ISd, Msb, K) and ",[2,"ثِخَنٌ"]," (Z, Msb, K) and ",[2,"ثُخْنٌ"],"; (TA;) ",[1,"It"]," (a thing, S, Msb) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, thick, big, gross,"]," or ",[1,"coarse;"]," and ",[1,"hard, firm, stiff, tough,"]," or ",[1,"strong:"]," (S, K:) ",[1,"it was,"]," or ",[1,"became, thick, dense,"]," or ",[1,"compact:"]," (M, TA:) [",[1,"it"]," (a garment, or piece of cloth,) ",[1,"was thick,"]," or ",[1,"close, in texture:"]," (see ",[2,"ثَخِينٌ"],":)] ",[1,"it"]," [a semiliquid of any kind] ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, thick, so that it did not flow, nor continue in its passing away."]," (Er-Rághib, TA.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"اثخنهُ","t":["[in its primary sense, ",[1,"He,"]," or ",[1,"it, rendered it"],[2,"ثَخِين"],", i. e. ",[1,"thick,"]," &c. ― -b2- And hence,] (tropical:) ",[1,"He,"]," or ",[1,"it,"]," (a man, JK, T, Mgh, Msb, and a wound, S, Mgh, and disease, Bd in viii. 68,) ",[1,"rendered him heavy:"]," (JK, T, Bd ubi suprà, TA:) or ",[1,"weakened him, rendered him languid,"]," or ",[1,"enervated him."]," (S, Mgh, Msb, K, TA.) You say, ",[2,"اثخنهُ ضَرْبًا"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He rendered him heavy by beating:"]," (JK:) or ",[1,"he beat him much,"]," or ",[1,"vehemently,"]," or ",[1,"excessively."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"أَثْخَنْتُهُ بِالجِراحَةِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"I weakened him, rendered him languid,"]," or ",[1,"enervated him, by the wound,"]," or ",[1,"wounds."]," (Msb.) ― -b3- ",[2,"إِذَا أَثْخَنْتُمُوهُمْ"],", in the Kur xlvii. 4, means (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"When ye have made much slaughter among them:"]," (Jel:) or ",[1,"when ye have made a great and vehement slaughter of them:"]," (Bd:) or ",[1,"when ye have overcome them, and wounded them much,"]," or ",[1,"inflicted many wounds upon them,"]," (Abu-l-'Abbás, K, TA,) ",[1,"so that they give with their hands."]," (Abu-l-'Abbás, TA.) ― -b4- ",[2,"اثخن فِى العَدُوِّ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He made a great,"]," or ",[1,"vehement, slaughter,"]," (A,) or ",[1,"a great,"]," or ",[1,"vehement, wounding,"]," (K,) ",[1,"among the enemy."]," (A, K.) ― -b5- ",[2,"اثخن فِى الأَرْضِ"],", (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He made much slaughter in the earth,"]," or ",[1,"land:"]," (Bd in viii. 68, Mgh, TA: in the S, ",[2,"اثخن فِى الأَرْضِ قَتْلًا"],", which means the same: TA:) or ",[1,"he went against the enemy, and made a wide,"]," or ",[1,"large, slaughter of them"]," [",[1,"in the land"],"]: (Msb:) or ",[1,"he fought vehemently in the earth,"]," or ",[1,"land."]," (Jel in viii. 68.) ― -b6- ",[2,"اثخن فِى الأَمْرِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He exceeded the usual,"]," or ",[1,"the just, bounds,"]," or ",[1,"degree, in the affair; strove,"]," or ",[1,"exerted himself, vigorously,"]," or ",[1,"strenuously, therein;"]," or ",[1,"did his utmost therein."]," (TA.) ― -b7- ",[2,"اثخنهُ قُوْلُهُ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"His saying took,"]," or ",[1,"had, an effect upon him;"]," or ",[1,"distressed,"]," or ",[1,"afflicted, him."]," (TA.) ― -b8- ",[2,"أَثْخَنْتُ فُلَانًا مَعْرِفَةً"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"I knew such a one,"]," or ",[1,"was acquainted with him, thoroughly,"]," or ",[1,"very well."]," (TA.)"],"f":"4"},{"h":"اثّخن","t":["in the saying of El-Asshà, ",[2,"تَمَهَّلَ فِى الحَرْبِ حَتَّى ٱثَّخَنَ"]," [",[1,"He acted deliberately in war until he became heavy,"]," or ",[1,"weakened,"]," or ",[1,"languid,"]," or ",[1,"enervated, by wounds"],"], is contracted by idghám from ",[2,"اثْتَخَنَ"],". (S, TA.)"],"f":"8"},{"h":"استثخن مِنْهُ النَّوْمُ","t":["(tropical:) ",[1,"Sleep overcame him."]," (JK, K, TA.) ",[2,"استثخن بَيْنَ المَرَضِ وَالإِعْيَآءِ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He became overcome by"]," [lit. ",[1,"between"],"] ",[1,"disease and fatigue."]," (A, TA.)"],"f":"10"},{"h":"ثُخْنٌ","t":["an inf. n. of ",[2,"ثَخُنَ"],": [commonly used as a simple subst., meaning ",[1,"Thickness,"]," &c.:] one says ",[2,"ثُوْبٌ لَهُ ثُخْنٌ"]," [",[1,"A garment,"]," or ",[1,"piece of cloth, having thickness,"]," or ",[1,"closeness, of texture"],"]. (TA.)"]},{"h":"ثَخَنٌ","t":["i. q. ",[2,"نقلة"]," [app. a mistranscription for ",[2,"ثَقْلَةٌ"]," or ",[2,"ثَقَلَةٌ"],", meaning (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A heaviness in the chest"]," or ",[1,"body,"]," or ",[1,"a heaviness and langour,"]," or ",[1,"a heaviness on the heart"],"]; as also ↓ ",[2,"ثَخَنَةٌ"],": El-'Ajjáj says, ",[2,"حَتَّى يَعِجَّ ثَخَنًا مَنْ عَجْعَجَا"]," [app. meaning ",[1,"So that he who cries out cries out by reason of heaviness,"]," &c.]: (TA: [this saying is also cited in the S, in art. ",[2,"عج"],"; but there, in one copy, I find ",[2,"ثَخِنًا"],"; and in another, ",[2,"ثِخَنًا"],"; and in both, ",[2,"مِنْ"]," instead of ",[2,"مَنْ"],":]) and hence he received the surname of ",[2,"العَجَّاج"],": (S and TA in art. ",[2,"عج"],":) so says IDrd. (TA in that art.) [Golius explains ",[2,"ثَخَنٌ"]," as meaning “ crassities, spissitudo; ” on the anthority of Ibn-Maaroof and Ibn-Beytár; but I suspect that he found ",[2,"ثَخَنٌ"]," in their works written for ",[2,"ثُخْنٌ"]," or ",[2,"ثِخَنٌ"],", both inf. ns. of ",[2,"ثَخُنَ"],".]"]},{"h":"ثَخَنَةٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"ثَخُنٌ"],"."]},{"h":"ثَخِينٌ","t":["part. n. of ",[2,"ثَخُنَ"],"; (S, Msb;) ",[1,"Thick, big, coarse,"]," or ",[1,"gross;"]," and ",[1,"hard, firm, stiff, tough,"]," or ",[1,"strong:"]," (S:) [",[1,"thick, dense,"]," or ",[1,"compact:"]," &c.: see 1: pl. ",[2,"ثِخَانٌ"],".] You say ",[2,"ثَوْبٌ ثَخِينٌ"],[1,"A garment,"]," or ",[1,"piece of cloth, thick,"]," or ",[1,"close,"]," or ",[1,"full, in texture,"]," and, as Az adds, ",[1,"in warp."]," (TA.) ― -b2- Applied to a man, ",[1,"Completely armed:"]," (KL:) or ",[2,"ثَخِينُ السِّلَاحِ"]," has this meaning. (S.) ― -b3- Also (JK, TA) (tropical:) ",[1,"Forbearing, clement, grave, sedate,"]," or ",[1,"calm:"]," (JK, K, * TA: [in some copies of the K, ",[2,"الحَكِيمُ"]," is erroneously put for ",[2,"الحَلِيمُ"],":]) in the M, ",[1,"heavy in his sitting-place."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"مُثْخَنٌ","t":["[pass. part. n. of 4, q. v.]. You say, ",[2,"تَرَكْتُهُ مُثْخَنًا وَقِيذًا"]," [",[1,"I left him weakened, languid, enervated,"]," or ",[1,"much wounded; beaten until he was at the point of death"],"]. (TA.) ― -b2- (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Forbearing, clement, grave, sedate,"]," or ",[1,"calm, in mind,"]," or ",[1,"intellect."]," (TA.) [See also ",[2,"ثَخِينٌ"],".] ― -b3- Metonymically applied by the people of Syria to (tropical:) One ",[1,"who causes laughter; who is quick, brisk,"]," or ",[1,"lively, in his motions."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"مُثْخِنٌ","t":["(assumed tropical:) One ",[1,"who exceeds the usual,"]," or ",[1,"the just, bounds,"]," or ",[1,"who does his utmost, in narration, and in the rehearsal of sayings."]," (TA.) ― -b2- And, with ",[2,"ة"],", (tropical:) A ",[1,"large, corpulent, fleshy,"]," woman. (JK, A, K.)"]}]},"maqayis":["الثاء والخاء والنون يدل على رزانة الشيء في ثقل. تقول ثخن الشيء ثخانة. والرجل الحليم الرزين ثخين. والثوب المكتنز اللحمة والسدى من جودة نسجه ثخين. وقد أثخنته أي أثقلته، قال الله تعالى: {حتى يثخن في الأرض} [الأنفال: 67] ، وذلك أن القتيل قد أثقل حتى لا حراك به. وتركته مثخنا، أي وقيذا. وقال قوم: يقال للأعزل الذي لا سلاح معه: ثخين ; وهو قياس الباب، لأن حركته تقل، خوفا على نفسه."],"mufradat":["يقال ثخن الشيء فهو ثخين: إذا غلظ فلم يسل، ولم يستمر في ذهابه، ومنه استعير قولهم: أثخنته ضربا واستخفافا. قال الله تعالى: ما كان لنبي أن يكون له أسرى حتى يثخن في الأرض [الأنفال/ 67] ، حتى إذا أثخنتموهم فشدوا الوثاق [محمد/ 4] ."]}